  {
    "id": 3972357635,
    "type": null,
    "body": "Closed by MR !27, merged on 2026-10-07 as merge commit `f26c9b0ed`. The plan's record is closed in\n`0b88bb81d`.\n\n- `d989a8517`: once `extract_char_final()` has dropped a character's objects in the room, it\n  writes the character's object save again, so the next login does not bring back what the room\n  holds. `Crash_delete_crashfile()`, which was meant to do that, is a no-op under `OBJSAVE_DB`.\n- `be819da53`: `extract_char_final()` takes each bagged object out of its own bag and puts it in\n  the room, as it does the carried and worn ones, and the move names the right bag.\n  `objsave_save_and_extract()` extracts each bag's objects after the worn ones.\n  `empty_bags_to_inventory()` is gone.\n- `0980ae2dc` and, from the review, `f14da1d13`: `sortto`, `sortfrom`, `bags`, `put <item> bagN`\n  and `get <item|all> bagN` answer \"You have no bags.\" for a character without bag storage\n  instead of ending the server.\n- Review, `edf0ce122`: `get_char_bag()` answers NULL for a character without bag storage, so the\n  extraction loop survives a player body built by a staff command. The pre-existing `stat file`\n  defect it met is #32.\n- Review, `f6e48f0e9`: the empty save of a leave without a save is tried twice, as the leaving\n  saves are, and the staff are told after two failures.\n- `docs/systems/SAVE_SYSTEMS_BREAKDOWN.md` says what the leaving saves take along and what a leave\n  without a save does.\n- No deploy: the fix reaches production with the next release.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
      "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
    },
